From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:18:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Keep a start_disabled BSS quiet on interface enable

A BSS with start_disabled=1 starts without Beacon frames. They start
with the first Beacon update that is requested for the BSS, for example
by UPDATE_BEACON or RELOAD.

If the driver disables the interface before that and enables it again,
hostapd_iface_enable() calls ieee802_11_set_beacon() for every started
BSS. The Beacon frames of the start_disabled BSS then start without a
request.

Skip the Beacon update on interface enable for a start_disabled BSS
whose Beacon frames were never set since the BSS setup. Track this in
its own flag, since beacon_set_done is cleared when the driver reports
NL80211_CMD_STOP_AP on interface disable. A start_disabled BSS that
beacons before the interface disable starts beaconing again on enable.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/ap/beacon.c
+++ b/src/ap/beacon.c
@@ -2768,6 +2768,7 @@ static int __ieee802_11_set_beacon(struc
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211AX */
 
 	hapd->beacon_set_done = 1;
+	hapd->beacon_started = 1;
 
 	if (ieee802_11_build_ap_params(hapd, &params) < 0)
 		return -1;
--- a/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
+++ b/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
@@ -2542,7 +2542,8 @@ static void hostapd_iface_enable(struct
 		else
 			hostapd_reconfig_encryption(hapd);
 		hapd->reenable_beacon = 1;
-		ieee802_11_set_beacon(hapd);
+		if (!hapd->conf->start_disabled || hapd->beacon_started)
+			ieee802_11_set_beacon(hapd);
 #ifdef NEED_AP_MLME
 	} else if (hapd->disabled && hapd->iface->cac_started) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "DFS: restarting pending CAC");
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -523,6 +523,7 @@ void hostapd_free_hapd_data(struct hosta
 	}
 	hapd->started = 0;
 	hapd->beacon_set_done = 0;
+	hapd->beacon_started = 0;
 
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "%s(%s)", __func__, hapd->conf->iface);
 	accounting_deinit(hapd);
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.h
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.h
@@ -200,6 +200,7 @@ struct hostapd_data {
 	unsigned int started:1;
 	unsigned int disabled:1;
 	unsigned int reenable_beacon:1;
+	unsigned int beacon_started:1;
 
 	u8 own_addr[ETH_ALEN];
 
